{"turn": 95, "elapsed_s": 1808.3, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "text": "Output file written and validated. Here is the complete hypothesis inventory for the **Core \u2194 Pool Type** boundary:\n\n---\n\n## Hypothesis Summary: Core \u2194 Pool Type Boundary\n\n**File**: `docs/targets/full-system/artifacts/pass1-core-pooltype/hypotheses-core-pooltype.json`\n\n| ID | Confidence | Location | Mechanism | Actionability |\n|----|-----------|----------|-----------|---------------|\n| **H-CPT-001** | MEDIUM | `DynamicHelper` L396-399 | Per-tick `mulDivRoundingUp` protocol fee accumulates up to N extra wei vs `_validateProtocolFees` floor check; LP feeGrowthGlobal understated by same amount | Confirmed structurally; magnitude \u2264 N wei (N = tick crossings). Not directly extractable by swapper. |\n| **H-CPT-002** | MEDIUM | `FixedHelper.normalizePriceToRatio` L1114-1126 | Two sequential `mulDiv` (floor) compound truncation \u2192 ratio0 biased DOWN by \u22642 LSBs; oracle-initialized pools have skewed exchange rate. **Same bug class as accepted finding CP-006.** | **Priority: verify call sites.** If called during pool init from Dynamic oracle, likely submittable. |\n| **H-CPT-003** | LOW | `FixedHelper._splitAmountsAndFeesByHeight` L1684-1691 | `tmpSwapCache` dead write \u2014 recalculated fees for `totalAmountInFilled` never written back; fee split uses stale `swapCache.lpFeeAmount` | Same class as FP-SUB03 (already rejected). Do not submit. |\n| **H-CPT-004** | MEDIUM | `FixedHelper.swapByInput` L910-930 | Fallback to output-mode changes fee formula at reserve exhaustion boundary; \u00b11 wei fee difference at the threshold | Invariant break. Not economically material (1 wei). |\n| **H-CPT-005** | MEDIUM | `SwapMath.computeSwapByOutputStep` L143 vs `computeSwapByInputStep` L73 | Output swaps always use ceiling fee; input swaps use exact arithmetic for final partial-fill step \u2192 output swaps pay up to N extra wei vs equivalent input swaps | Structural asymmetry. Users should route as input swaps to minimize fees. Not a vulnerability per se. |\n| **H-CPT-006** | MEDIUM | `AMMModule._validateProtocolFees` L1654-1677 | Floor-based minimum threshold allows pool types to report floor-rounded protocol fees; combined with H-CPT-001 ceiling accumulation, these effects are directionally opposing | Design tolerance, not exploitable with registered pool types (6-leading-zero-bytes guard). |\n\n### Priority Action\n**Investigate H-CPT-002 immediately.** `FixedHelper.normalizePriceToRatio` uses two sequential `FullMath.mulDiv` calls with floor rounding \u2014 the identical pattern to CP-006 (CLOBHelper, accepted Medium). If this function is called on the oracle price initialization path for Fixed pools, it is a second instance of the same confirmed vulnerability."}]}
